adjudication.rationale:
In GoogleCalendarService.deleteEvent the new fallback logic is:

const calendarId = externalCalendarId ? externalCalendarId : event.destinationCalendar?.find((cal) => cal.externalId === externalCalendarId)?.externalId;

When externalCalendarId is null/undefined (the exact case the fallback is meant to handle), the find() predicate compares cal.externalId to null/undefined, which will almost always return no match, yielding undefined. The subsequent use of `calendarId || defaultCalendarId` therefore falls back to "primary" even when `event.destinationCalendar` contains the correct externalId, changing behavior from the pre-refactor version (`... : event.destinationCalendar?.externalId`). This can cause deletions to target the wrong calendar and leave the real event undeleted.
